# 6. India plumbing
c('india', 'Exotel is a first-class provider since 2026-06-01: Exotel Voicebot applet streams 8 kHz PCM over WebSocket to wss://api(.in.residency).elevenlabs.io/v1/convai/conversation/exotel; outbound uses Exotel Calls/connect with the customer\'s API key/token; Mumbai (api.in.exotel.com) and Singapore clusters; Voicebot applet is gated and needs Exotel support (1-2 business days); transfers need a chained Connect applet.', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__phone-numbers__telephony__exotel.md', D + 'changelog/entries/2026-6-1.md', D + 'openapi/api.elevenlabs.io_openapi.json')
c('india', 'India data residency exists as an Enterprise-only isolated environment (in.residency.elevenlabs.io, separate workspace and API key); storage is in India but "processing may nevertheless occur outside", Realtime v1 Max is unavailable there, and agents must be recreated (no migration). This corrects the 2026-10-17 parity row "Data residency page (EU/US); no India region found".', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/overview__administration__data-residency.md', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__customization__realtime-models.md', 'research/2026-10-17/lanes/l4a-competitors/parity.csv')
c('india', 'Across 258 saved agents/overview docs pages there is no mention of TRAI, DLT, NCPR/DND, 140/160-series or Indian calling hours; the only telemarketing-law page is TCPA (US). Batch calling has no calling-window, DNC or consent field; the TCPA page tells the buyer to keep DNC lists, honour 8am-9pm and record consent. India compliance is left to the buyer (confirms ledger CMP-27).', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__legal__tcpa.md', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__phone-numbers__batch-calls.md', 'research/2026-10-17/ledger.md')
c('india', 'AI disclosure and recording consent are a contractual duty of the buyer (ElevenAgents terms): notice must precede any interaction; the sample verbal line is "Hi, I\'m an AI assistant. This call may be recorded...". The platform does not inject it.', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__legal__disclosure-requirement.md')
c('india', 'The India marketing page claims voices "tuned for Indian accents and code-switched speech", 12 Indian languages and accents in the voice library, Hinglish tuning, Ozonetel/Exotel/Plivo integrations, forward-deployed engineering, India residency, SOC 2 Type II/ISO 27001/PCI DSS L1, and Indian agent customers Meesho, Cars24 and TVS Motor. No benchmark is published; "Hinglish" appears nowhere in the docs.', 'vendor-claimed', D + 'india/elevenlabs.io_india.txt', D + 'docs-md/overview__models.md')
c('india', 'Twilio regional routing supports only us1/ie1/au1 region IDs in the API; Twilio numbers default to us1 even for non-US numbers. An Indian buyer on Twilio is therefore routed through the US (Twilio also allows outbound to India only from non-Indian numbers, per the vapi lane).', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__phone-numbers__twilio-integration__regional-routing.md', D + 'openapi/api.elevenlabs.io_openapi.json')
c('india', 'ASR and TTS language lists include Hindi, Bengali, Gujarati, Kannada, Malayalam, Marathi, Odia, Punjabi, Tamil, Telugu, Urdu and Assamese; language switching mid-call needs the language-detection system tool, which is off by default and is triggered by the LLM.', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/overview__models.md', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__customization__tools__system-tools__language-detection.md')
# 7. Failure modes
c('failures', 'Measured on 2026-10-17 (l4b, homepage demo, US vantage): clean-turn p50 3.75 s (n=63), end-of-turn transcript p50 2.65 s (n=72), Hindi callers answered in English, "hmm"/"haan" answered with "Are you still there?" on 4/16 short turns, barge-in handled 3/7, a babble session slowed to 8 s and dropped. These are the strongest failure observations available without an account.', 'observed', 'research/2026-10-17/lanes/l4b-measured/report.md', 'research/2026-10-17/lanes/l4b-measured/data/elevenlabs-ws-timing.csv')
c('failures', 'Trustpilot: TrustScore 3.0 from 1,192 reviews. Agent-relevant complaints (filtered "agent", WebFetch summary): support unreachable or AI-only ("routes to an AI agent that cannot resolve billing matters and does not transfer to a person", 2026-06-11; "customer support? Non-existent", 2025-12-01), docs ("confusing docs", "brute force an agent at the dashboard and API to figure it out", 2026-10-06), dropped calls without memory ("the call unexpectedly drops out ... answers with no record of the previous conversation", 2026-06-17), WhatsApp integration failing with unanswered tickets (2026-01-12), credits charged for agent mistakes (2026-07-24).', 'observed', D + 'complaints/trustpilot-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt')
c('failures', 'GitHub elevenlabs/packages: 232 issues; the most-discussed are SDK connection/state bugs (#635 agent connects but does not speak, #152 "could not establish pc connection", #257 first WebSocket connection often fails, #143 conversation stays active after endSession, #336 agent stuck in listening mode, #47 request for silence_duration_ms control).', 'observed', D + 'complaints/github-packages-issues-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt')
c('failures', 'Retell community threads (in l4a complaints.csv) about ElevenLabs as a TTS inside Retell: v3 stutter, sentences skipped, v3 billing by generated speech vs call duration, cost of ElevenLabs TTS; 12 of 869 coded items.', 'observed', 'research/2026-10-17/lanes/l4a-competitors/complaints.csv')
c('failures', 'HN (Algolia, 211 comments since 2025-10): few agent complaints; one says "Elevenlabs using a completely incapable voice agent for sales outreach made me wonder if they were actively trying to dissuade customers" (2026-05-10, item 48088509); one on billing lock-in to a Google account (2026-04-05, item 47653609). An ElevenLabs employee says they chose a cascading model "because it\'s better suited for enterprise use cases" (2025-12-11, item 46236377).', 'observed', D + 'complaints/hn-filtered.json')
c('failures', 'Complaint code profile for ElevenAgents from accessible sources: SUPPORT and DOCS/UX dominate review text; RELIABILITY shows in SDK issues and 9 agent/telephony incidents in 75 days; CONVERSATION (latency, language hold, backchannels) shows only in our own measurements. Reddit, G2 and the GitHub API were blocked (403) and were not bypassed, so this profile is thin.', 'inferred', D + 'complaints/trustpilot-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt', D + 'complaints/github-packages-issues-webfetch-2026-10-20.txt', D + 'status/incidents-parsed.json')
# 8. v2 notes
c('v2', 'Memory across calls is not documented publicly, but the data model has memory entries (MemoryEntrySearchResult with version and a source of conversation or manual; LoadableMemoryEntry; resource type convai_memory_entries) and the dashboard bundle calls /v1/convai/agents/{id}/memories CRUD and /agents/{id}/user-memory/preview. Memory is in development or private beta (inference).', 'observed', D + 'openapi/api.elevenlabs.io_openapi.json', T + 'bundle-endpoints.json', D + 'changelog/entries/2026-6-15.md')
c('v2', 'Personalisation today is per-call: dynamic variables, per-conversation overrides (prompt, first message, language, voice), user_id for grouping conversations, and Twilio inbound personalisation webhooks; nothing carries facts from one call to the next without the buyer\'s own store (the docs recommend summarising history from post-call webhooks).', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__customization__personalization.md', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__customization__llm__optimizing-costs.md')
c('v2', 'The optimisation loop is human-gated: Spotlight finds patterns, Architect proposes a branch with tests, a teammate approves the merge proposal, and experiments split traffic deterministically by conversation id and the user promotes the winner by hand (no significance test is documented). "Proactive proposals" and scheduled automations are announced as coming; the bundle already calls /convai/automations and /triage-tickets/{id}/architect-dispatches.', 'observed', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__operate__architect__faq.md', D + 'docs-md/eleven-agents__operate__experiments.md', T + 'bundle-endpoints.json')
